The original public certificate files are retained without alteration.
Bundles concatenate those files for explicit application-level selection.
No endorsement, affiliation, automatic trust or legal acceptance is implied.

OpenSSL does not support v7's Ed521 algorithm (OID1.3.6.1.4.1.44588.2.1).
Its original file is retained only under reference-ed521, not in any bundle.
The other seven roots have native OpenSSL self-signature and validity checks.
No v7 self-signature or Ed521 identification workflow is certified here.
Algorithm/fingerprint reference: ITI WebTrust report, Appendix A (2019):
https://www.gov.br/iti/pt-br/assuntos/comite-gestor/iti_2019_-_webtrust_for_ca_report_consolidado.pdf

Included versions: v4, v5, v6, v7, v10, v11, v12, v13.
Registry purposes: v10 TLS; v11 code signing; other included roots general
ICP-Brasil certificates. An application still needs its own document policy.
Excluded expired versions: v0, v1, v2.
Excluded revoked versions: v3, v8, v9.

This is a dated root dataset, not the complete CA chain archive, a CRL cache
or an online verification service. Installation changes no certificate store.
